      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Louis Park was incorporated as a village in 1886, and its post office was called 'Elmwood' from 1887 to 1890.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Louis_Park%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from the Minneapolis and St. Louis Railway; 'Park' was added to avoid confusion with another St. Louis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Louis_Park%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1890s, the Moline Plow Company factory near downtown employed over 600 workers, making the village a hub for agricultural equipment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
